.TH "gtk4-node-editor" "1" "" "GTK" "GTK commands"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
gtk4-node-editor \- View and edit render node files
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.nf
\fBgtk4\-node\-editor\fP [OPTIONS...] [FILE]
.fi
.sp
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
\fBgtk4\-node\-editor\fP is a utility to show and edit render node files.
Such render node files can be obtained e.g. from the GTK inspector or
as part of the testsuite in the GTK sources.
.sp
\fBgtk4\-node\-editor\fP is used by GTK developers for debugging and testing,
and it has built\-in support for saving testcases as part of the GTK testsuite.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.sp
\fB\-h, \-\-help\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Show the application help.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-version\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Show the program version.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fB\-\-reset\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Don\(aqt restore autosaved content and remove autosave files.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH "محیط (ENVIRONMENT)"
.sp
\fBGTK_SOURCE_DIR\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
can be set to point to the location where the GTK sources reside, so that
testcases can be saved to the right location. If unsed, \fIgtk4\-node\-editor\(ga\fP
checks if the current working directory looks like a GTK checkout, and failing
that, saves testcase in the the current working directory.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
